From: RK3588 voice engine project
Subject: [PATCH] rknpu: adapt 0.9.8 to Ubuntu Rockchip 1025 on RK3588

Apply after extracting Rockchip's rknpu_driver_0.9.8_20241009.tar.bz2
over Joshua-Riek/linux-rockchip at Ubuntu-rockchip-6.1.0-1025.25
(7348ed5de414cc11a9831d269963d4a62f60b00e).

That kernel lacks rockchip_opp_set_low_length. The reference is in the
RK3576 OPP data; RK3588 uses rk3588_npu_set_soc_info instead. Omit the
RK3576 callback for this RK3588/RK3588S-only backport. This patch is not
a supported RK3576 adaptation and does not establish runtime compatibility.

The original driver archive SHA-256 is:
188306a3eba7ca48c186fe2a39acf232dec8536484581e54e9b96c3f65677eba

--- a/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/rknpu/rknpu_devfreq.c
@@ -235,6 +235,5 @@
 static const struct rockchip_opp_data rk3576_npu_opp_data = {
 	.set_read_margin = rk3576_npu_set_read_margin,
-	.set_soc_info = rockchip_opp_set_low_length,
 #if KERNEL_VERSION(6, 1, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE
 	.config_regulators = npu_opp_config_regulators,
 	.config_clks = npu_opp_config_clks,
